[:div {:class "description"} [:p {} [:a {:href "/athletes/112272"} "Sarah Sjöström"] " (SWE) had first competed at the Olympic Games in 2008, as a 14-year-old. She was back for her fifth appearance and was still the world record holder in this event, set at the 2017 World Championships. At 30-years-old, she was considered ancient for a world-class swimmer and was not considered a gold medal contender in 2024. Apparently, Sarah Sjöström never got that message."] "\n\n" [:p {} [:a {:href "/athletes/129061"} "Emma McKeon"] " was the defending gold medalist but only made the Australian team in the 100 metre butterfly. In her absence, the favorites were considered to be her teammate " [:a {:href "/athletes/140694"} "Mollie O’Callaghan"] ", the 2022 and 2023 World Champion; " [:a {:href "/athletes/130494"} "Siobhán Haughey"] " (HKG), the silver medalist from Tokyo 2020; and " [:a {:href "/athletes/131199"} "Marrit Steenbergen"] " (NED), the 2024 World Champion."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The three favorites made the final, along with Sjöström, and " [:a {:href "/athletes/147283"} "Torri Huske"] ", the Americans’ top hope who had already taken gold in Paris in the 100 fly. Huske was out fastest and led at 50 metres, but Sjöström was only 2/10ths of a second behind, although in fourth place at that point. O’Callaghan got out slowly and was tied for last place at the turn."] "\n\n" [:p {} "O’Callaghan had the fastest second lap but it would only bring her home in fourth. Sjöström closed on Huske with the second-best final lap and out-touched the American to win a surprising gold medal. Haughey held on to take the bronze."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Sjöström came to Paris expecting to swim only the 50 metre freestyle, and relays, but added the 100 free at the last minute. She later said, “I never thought I would win a gold medal at my fifth Olympics.” Four days later, she would shock the swimming world again, winning the 50 metre freestyle, giving her six Olympic medals, three of them gold – she won the 100 butterfly in 2016. Although many swimmers had won more Olympic medals, most of them did it with the benefit of relay medals, but Sweden was not a swimming powerhouse, and all of Sjöström’s medals were in individual events."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/112272"} "Sarah Sjöström"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/SWE"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/SWE.png"}] "SWE"]] [:td {} "52.99 (1 h2)"] [:td {} "52.87 (3 h2)"] [:td {} "52.16 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/147283"} "Torri Huske"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "53.53 (3 h4)"] [:td {} "52.99 (4 h2)"] [:td {} "52.29 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/130494"} "Siobhán Haughey"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/HKG"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/HKG.png"}] "HKG"]] [:td {} "53.02 (1 h4)"] [:td {} "52.64 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "52.33 (3)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "4"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/140694"} "Mollie O'Callaghan"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/AUS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/AUS.png"}] "AUS"]] [:td {} "53.27 (1 h3)"] [:td {} "52.75 (1 h2)"] [:td {} "52.34 (4)"]